/S /H2
/P 165 0 R
/T (So What Is Explainable AI, Really?)
/E (So What Is Explainable AI, Really?)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [14]
>>
endobj
401 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 165 0 R
/E ( Explainable AI is a collection of methods for making machine-learning predictions easier to interpret. Instead of simply accepting an output, XAI asks what factors contributed to it and whether changing important inputs would change the result. [3][4])
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [15]
>>
endobj
402 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 165 0 R
/E ( Some approaches explain individual predictions, while others show how a model behaves more broadly. The important distinction is that an explanation should be useful, not just visually impressive. A simple explanation that helps someone challenge a wrong prediction can be more valuable than one that only looks convincing. [1][2][3])
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [16]
>>
endobj
