529 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 171 0 R
/E (Modern enterprises are becoming increasingly connected through cloud platforms, Internet of Things \(IoT\) devices, and industrial automation. That connectivity brings efficiency, but it also creates more places for attackers to enter. Data-driven cybersecurity responds to this challenge by combining large-scale data analysis, artificial intelligence, machine learning, and real-time monitoring to detect threats earlier and respond faster. This article looks at how these technologies work together, where they are used, and the practical challenges involved in building security systems that can learn and adapt as threats change. [1])
/Pg 26 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
530 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 171 0 R
/T (Data-Driven Cybersecurity Framework for Smart Enterprise Systems)
/E (Data-Driven Cybersecurity Framework for Smart Enterprise Systems)
/Pg 26 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
531 0 obj
<<
