>>
endobj
532 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 171 0 R
/E ( Traditional security tools often rely on predefined rules and known signatures. They remain useful, but they can struggle when an attack looks different from anything seen before. Data-driven cybersecurity takes a different approach: it continuously collects security data, analyzes patterns, and uses machine-learning models to identify unusual behavior. Instead of only reacting after an incident, the aim is to recognize warning signs early enough to prevent or limit the damage. [5])
/Pg 26 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
