558 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 172 0 R
/E ( The more connected an enterprise becomes, the harder it is to understand what is happening across the entire system. Data-driven security helps by bringing information from different sources together and looking for relationships between events. An unusual login, unexpected network traffic, and abnormal activity on an IoT device might look harmless individually, but together they can form a much stronger warning signal. [5])
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
559 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 172 0 R
/E ( Another advantage is the ability to look forward rather than only backward. Machine-learning systems can identify anomalies and use patterns from previous activity to estimate where vulnerabilities or attacks may develop. )
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
560 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 172 0 R
/E (This is particularly valuable in environments such as healthcare, finance, and smart manufacturing, where a security incident can affect both sensitive information and physical operations. [4])
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [13]
>>
endobj
