654 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 177 0 R
/E ( The next stage of TinyML is likely to move beyond simply running a trained model on a small device. Researchers are exploring ways for devices to adapt locally, while federated learning could allow multiple devices to improve models collectively without directly sharing raw data. [1][3])
/Pg 32 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
655 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 177 0 R
/E ( Energy harvesting is another promising direction. If devices can draw power from light, heat, or movement, TinyML systems could remain active for long periods in remote locations. Specialized low-power hardware and more standardized frameworks could also make deployment easier across different platforms. [1][3][4])
/Pg 32 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
656 0 obj
<<
