662 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 177 0 R
/E ( TinyML changes the way we think about where artificial intelligence has to live. Instead of depending entirely on large servers, useful intelligence can be placed directly inside the small devices already surrounding us. This makes real-time, private, and offline decision-making possible where sending data to the cloud is slow, expensive, or impractical. [1][3])
/Pg 32 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
