>>
endobj
680 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 178 0 R
/T (Climate-Conscious Computing: Creating Algorithms with the Environment in Mind)
/E (Climate-Conscious Computing: Creating Algorithms with the Environment in Mind)
/Pg 33 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
681 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 178 0 R
/E ( Computers are now part of almost everything we do, from communication and banking to healthcare and scientific research. But behind these services are data centers, networks, and increasingly large AI models that require significant amounts of energy. The digital revolution has brought enormous benefits, but its environmental cost is becoming part of the conversation [1][2][3].)
/Pg 33 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
682 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 178 0 R
/E ( This is where climate-conscious computing comes in. Instead of treating sustainability as something to think about after a system is built, it makes environmental impact part of the design itself. An algorithm should ideally be judged not only by how quickly or accurately it works, but also by how much unnecessary computation it requires [1][3].)
/Pg 33 0 R
/K [13]
>>
endobj
683 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 178 0 R
/T (The Computing Energy Cost)
/E (The Computing Energy Cost)
/Pg 33 0 R
/K [14]
>>
endobj
