3830 0 obj
<<
/Title (Data-driven cybersecurity represents a shift in how modern enterprises approach security. Instead of waiting for a known attack and then reacting to it, organizations can continuously collect information, identify unusual behavior, assess risk, and automate parts of the response. Big data analytics, machine learning, SIEM, and automated security platforms each contribute a different piece to this process.)
/Dest [28 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 3824 0 R
/Next 3831 0 R
>>
endobj
3831 0 obj
<<
/Title (At the same time, the technology is not a magic shield. Data quality, computing requirements, false alarms, explainability, cost, and privacy can all limit its effectiveness. The real value comes from building a system that combines intelligent automation with human oversight and continuous learning.)
/Dest [28 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 3824 0 R
/Prev 3830 0 R
>>
endobj
3832 0 obj
<<
/Title (CASC-M | VOL.7, ISSUE 3 |MAY JUNE, 2026)
