3836 0 obj
<<
/Title (The idea sounds straightforward, but building a reliable data-driven security system is not. The first challenge is scale. Enterprises can generate enormous amounts of security data from many different sources, and processing all of it in real time requires substantial)
/Dest [28 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 3829 0 R
/Next 3842 0 R
>>
endobj
3837 0 obj
<<
/Title (Cost is another practical barrier. Effective data-driven cybersecurity requires infrastructure, specialized expertise, continuous maintenance, and regular model updates. Finally, collecting and analyzing large amounts of user and system data creates privacy concerns. Strong security therefore has to be balanced with responsible data handling and appropriate access controls. [4])
/Dest [28 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 3829 0 R
/Prev 3843 0 R
>>
endobj
3838 0 obj
<<
/Title (Abstract)
/Dest [25 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 3834 0 R
/Next 3844 0 R
>>
endobj
3839 0 obj
<<
/Title (Cyber Threat Detection and Response Lifecycle)
/Dest [27 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 3845 0 R
/First 3846 0 R
/Last 3846 0 R
/Count -1
/Next 3835 0 R
>>
endobj
3840 0 obj
<<
/Title (Machine-learning-based Intrusion Detection Systems \(IDS\) are an important part of this approach. They examine network traffic and system logs for patterns that may indicate suspicious behavior. The process generally begins with data collection, followed by feature extraction, where useful characteristics such as traffic flow, protocols, or other system attributes are selected. [5])
/Dest [28 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 3835 0 R
/Next 3847 0 R
>>
endobj
3841 0 obj
<<
/Title (The major advantage is adaptability. Instead of depending entirely on a fixed list of known attack signatures, machine-learning systems can learn patterns from data and potentially identify unusual activity that does not exactly match previously defined rules. That makes them particularly useful in environments where the threat landscape changes quickly. [5])
/Dest [28 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 3835 0 R
/Prev 3847 0 R
>>
endobj
3842 0 obj
<<
/Title (computing and storage resources. [6])
/Dest [28 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 3829 0 R
/Prev 3836 0 R
/Next 3843 0 R
>>
endobj
3843 0 obj
<<
/Title (Machine learning also introduces its own uncertainty. A model can produce false positives, miss an attack, or behave differently when it encounters data that is unlike its training data. Complex models can also be difficult to explain, which becomes a problem when security teams need to understand why a particular alert was generated. [3])
/Dest [28 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 3829 0 R
/Prev 3842 0 R
/Next 3837 0 R
>>
endobj
3844 0 obj
<<
/Title (Limitations and Risks)
/Dest [25 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 3838 0 R
/Next 3848 0 R
>>
endobj
